# What permissions.lua needs from outside Hammerspoon, declared beside the only file in
# this spoon that knows the tool. Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason.
# See Dependencies.spoon for the kinds and for how these files are found.
#
# Eyedropper declares this same compiler for its own helper. Both are kept, because a
# declaration belongs beside whatever knows the tool and neither spoon should have to
# learn that the other exists. The manifest carries a line per owner and the reconciler
# joins on the name, so one map entry answers both.
#
# Optional, matching Eyedropper, because a failed build is answered in the spoon's own
# words rather than by the root refusing to wire it.
swiftc | system | /usr/bin/swiftc | optional | builds the helper that asks for automation permission per browser
